{"task": "F1", "q": "Adaklu maize farmer planted late Feb, saw worms mid-March, sprayed the recommended chemicals with no effect. What next?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["chemical terms in question", "disease or pest terms in question", "no local reference for region 'adaklu' (coastal savannah zone; corpus covers Northern Ghana only for this question)", "citation check failed: 'The officer should inspect the field or refer the farmer to an expert for a proper diagno…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage lacks referral"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'The officer should inspect the field or refer the farmer to an expert for a proper diagno…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No match found"], "figures_checked": 0, "sentences_checked": 4, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The farmer should scout the maize field at least once a week, looking for unusual patterns such as insect damage, larvae, or stunted growth [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "If the infestation is severe and the recommended chemicals have not worked, the officer should consult the local Agricultural Extension Agent (AEA) for advice on the recommended fall armyworm control pesticide in the area [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Additionally, the farmer should consider rotating maize with non-host plants like groundnut, deep ploughing, and proper weeding to reduce future infestations [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "The officer should inspect the field or refer the farmer to an expert for a proper diagnosis.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No match found"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'The officer should inspect the field or refer the farmer to an expert for a proper diagno…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage lacks referral"], "figures_checked": 0, "sentences_checked": 3, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The officer should inspect the field or refer the farmer to an expert for a proper diagnosis [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passage lacks referral"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "The officer should consult the local Agricultural Extension Agent (AEA) for advice on the recommended fall armyworm control pesticide in the area [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The officer should also advise the farmer on preventive measures for the next season, such as rotating maize with non-host plants like groundnut, deep ploughing or burning infested maize residues, and proper weeding [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "The officer should inspect the field or refer the farmer to an expert for a proper diagnosis [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting]. The officer should consult the local Agricultural Extension Agent (AEA) for advice on the recommended fall armyworm control pesticide in the area [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control]. The officer should also advise the farmer on preventive measures for the next season, such as rotating maize with non-host plants like groundnut, deep ploughing or burning infested maize residues, and proper weeding [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention]."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nCaution: the curated sources cover Northern Ghana only. The guidance below comes from them and may not apply in Adaklu; the officer should confirm local timing.\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"It is recommended to have a walk through the maize field at least once a week. When scouting, walk through the field and look out for unusual patterns such as insect damage on leaves, cobs or stems, presence of insect larvae or eggs on maize leaves, abnormal leaf colour, and stunted slow growing plants.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting]\n- \"Rotate maize with non-host plants such as groundnut to help reduce Fall Army worm infestations. Deep ploughing and burial, or burning of infested maize residues helps to reduce populations in the following season. Proper weeding of maize fields also helps to reduce infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention]\n- \"Application of recommended pesticides can help to control infestations once they occur. Consult your local AEA for advice on the recommended fall army worm control pesticide in your area.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control]\n- \"Well dried and shelled maize should be treated with recommended storage chemicals and stored in jute sacks lined with polythene bags.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks]\nNote: The curated sources are for Northern Ghana; they may not apply in adaklu.\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible pest/disease: this is not a diagnosis. Officer should inspect or refer.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1668, "completion_tokens": 334}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1517, "completion_tokens": 161}}, "cost_usd": 0.000485}}
