{"task": "F4", "q": "Rains came late. Can I still plant maize in Northern Region at the end of July?", "auto": "FAIL", "auto_problems": ["citation check did not pass (verbatim fallback was used)"], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["sources differ on maize planting window: APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE", "citation check failed: 'early June' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major']; 'July 10th' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major']; 'early July' is not in the cited passage(s) ['IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major']; conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation; conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major]'s own figure is not state"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window", "IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties", "MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major", "IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major", "MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true], ["IITA-MAIZE-2025", true], ["MOFA-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'end of July' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant']", "'You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Adds claim"], "figures_checked": 8, "sentences_checked": 7, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use early maturing varieties.", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Adds claim"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Planting after the rains have stabilized will help avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Early maturing varieties such as Ewul-Boyu and Wang Dataa can be planted up to the end of July [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "One source says it should be between early June and July 10th [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "Another source says it should be from the end of May to early July [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major].", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 6, "sentence": "A third source says it should be from the end of May to the end of July [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major].", "cited": ["IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'early June' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major']", "'July 10th' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major']", "'early July' is not in the cited passage(s) ['IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major']", "conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation", "conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation", "'Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\"  says: \"Major seaso…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passages lack yields"], "figures_checked": 8, "sentences_checked": 6, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use early maturing varieties [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Plant after three good rains within the planting window [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains].", "cited": ["IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "[APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window] says: \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major] says: \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major] says: \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\"", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major", "IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passages lack yields"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use early maturing varieties [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties]. Plant after three good rains within the planting window [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains]. Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].\n\nSources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose. [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window] says: \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains. Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major] says: \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major] says: \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\""}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains. Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window]\n- \"It is recommended to plant after three good rains within the planting window to ensure enough soil moisture to support germination and early growth.\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains]\n- \"Early maturing varieties such as Ewul-Boyu and Wang Dataa can be planted up to end of July.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties]\n- \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major]\n- \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major]\n- \"Planting time or periods differ according to agro-ecology, season and maturity group of the variety. Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting. Planting time should be informed by local weather information.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant]\nNote: Sources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.\n\nNote: (officer only) Question received 25 Oct 2026. Windows cited: CSIR-SARI/APNI, northern region: between early June and July 10th; MoFA major season, guinea/sudan savannah: End of May-early July; IITA major season, guinea savannah: End of May - End of July. The date is outside the cited windows.\nNote: (officer only) No rainfall record: rainfall is looked up per district and 'Northern' is not a district AgriReach knows; ask the farmer which district they farm in.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1934, "completion_tokens": 468}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1581, "completion_tokens": 240}}, "cost_usd": 0.000589}}
{"task": "F5", "q": "Subsidised fertiliser arrived when the maize is knee-high, about two months after planting. Is it still worth applying?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "routine", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": [], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": true, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": true, "problems": [], "figures_checked": 2, "sentences_checked": 5, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The subsidised fertiliser can still be applied, but only if the soil is moist.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage implies"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Top dressing should be done when the soil is moist to enhance nutrient uptake [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The ideal time for top dressing is at 6 weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "If the soil is very dry, delay application until some rains are received [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "The basal application should have been applied at about two weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}]}}]}, "draft": "The subsidised fertiliser can still be applied, but only if the soil is moist. Top dressing should be done when the soil is moist to enhance nutrient uptake [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture]. The ideal time for top dressing is at 6 weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing]. If the soil is very dry, delay application until some rains are received [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture]. The basal application should have been applied at about two weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing].\n\nNote: (officer only) No rainfall record: the question names no district; ask the farmer which district they farm in.", "drafted_by": "model", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 637, "completion_tokens": 170}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 2200, "completion_tokens": 302}, "farmer_text": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 352, "completion_tokens": 81}}, "cost_usd": 0.000507}}
{"task": "F6", "q": "Weevils in maize stored three months in polypropylene sacks. How should I store the next harvest?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["disease or pest terms in question"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": true, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": true, "problems": [], "figures_checked": 2, "sentences_checked": 6, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Dry the maize immediately after harvest to reduce moisture content to 10-12% [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Shell the maize and remove the husks before storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Use jute sacks lined with polythene bags for storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}]}}]}, "draft": "To reduce weevil infestation in stored maize, follow these steps:\n\n1. Dry the maize immediately after harvest to reduce moisture content to 10-12% [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying].\n2. Shell the maize and remove the husks before storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling].\n3. Use jute sacks lined with polythene bags for storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "drafted_by": "model", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 679, "completion_tokens": 122}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1512, "completion_tokens": 139}, "farmer_text": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 299, "completion_tokens": 54}}, "cost_usd": 0.000331}}
{"task": "F7", "q": "Some of my stored maize is mouldy. Can I sell it or feed it to animals?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["food safety terms in question", "citation check failed: '15 ppb' states 15 ppb as an upper limit, but the cited passage(s) ['AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits'] give(s) it as a plain value; 'The European Union and the United States Food and Drugs Administration have lower limits…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Incorrect comparison; 'The officer should advise the farmer to test the maize for aflatoxin levels before decidi…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No advice given"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true], ["AGBETIAMEH-2018", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No disposal advice", "'The officer should advise the farmer to dispose of the mouldy maize safely.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No disposal advice"], "figures_checked": 1, "sentences_checked": 4, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No disposal advice"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Mould can indicate aflatoxin contamination, which has strict limits.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Aflatoxin limits"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The Ghana Standards Authority sets a limit of 15 ppb for maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "GSA limit stated"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "The officer should advise the farmer to dispose of the mouldy maize safely.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No disposal advice"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'15 ppb' states 15 ppb as an upper limit, but the cited passage(s) ['AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits'] give(s) it as a plain value", "'The European Union and the United States Food and Drugs Administration have lower limits…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Incorrect comparison", "'The officer should advise the farmer to test the maize for aflatoxin levels before decidi…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No advice given"], "figures_checked": 3, "sentences_checked": 4, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which have strict limits.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage implies"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "The Ghana Standards Authority allows up to 15 ppb of aflatoxins in maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The European Union and the United States Food and Drugs Administration have lower limits of 4 ppb and 20 ppb, respectively [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Incorrect comparison"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "The officer should advise the farmer to test the maize for aflatoxin levels before deciding to sell or feed it.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No advice given"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which have strict limits. The Ghana Standards Authority allows up to 15 ppb of aflatoxins in maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]. The European Union and the United States Food and Drugs Administration have lower limits of 4 ppb and 20 ppb, respectively [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]. The officer should advise the farmer to test the maize for aflatoxin levels before deciding to sell or feed it."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Maize should be stored after removal of maize husks and shelling. Storing unhusked maize is not recommended as it is very difficult to detect insect infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling]\n- \"Well dried and shelled maize should be treated with recommended storage chemicals and stored in jute sacks lined with polythene bags.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks]\n- \"At harvesting, maize grains are usually not fully dry and have a moisture content of about 15 to 20%. Immediately after harvesting, cobs should be dried so as to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% in readiness for storage.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying]\n- \"aflatoxin limits imposed by the European Union (4 ppb), the Ghana Standards Authority (GSA; 15 ppb for maize and 20 ppb for groundnut), and the United States Food and Drugs Administration (FDA; 20 ppb)\" [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible food-safety risk (mould/aflatoxin): AgriReach cannot clear produce for sale, food or feed. Officer should advise.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1647, "completion_tokens": 198}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1348, "completion_tokens": 189}}, "cost_usd": 0.000472}}
